  "beats": [
    {
      "t": "2026-11-04T00:00:01Z",
      "text": "On November 2, 2026, Bruce Springsteen announced his support for El-Sayed, calling him a fighter in defense of the U.S. Constitution and democracy against corrupt, anti-American leadership.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1384055642:95"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-04T00:00:08Z",
      "text": "El-Sayed faced Republican nominee Mike Rogers in the general election on November 3, 2026.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1384055642:68"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-04T00:00:15Z",
      "text": "Abdulrahman Mohamed El-Sayed, born October 31, 1984, is an American epidemiology professor, public health administrator, and politician who is the United States senator-elect from Michigan.",
      "cites": [
        "wiki:rev:1384055642:0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-04T00:00:25Z",
      "text": "Abdul El-Sayed was born on 31 October 1984 in Rochester Hills.",
      "cites": [
        "wd:Q25752879:P569",
        "wd:Q25752879:P19"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-04T00:00:33Z",
      "text": "He was educated at Andover High School, the University of Michigan College of Literature, Science, and the Arts, Columbia University Vagelos College of Physicians and Surgeons and Oriel College.",
      "cites": [
        "wd:Q25752879:P69:Q4754616",
        "wd:Q25752879:P69:Q7895753",
        "wd:Q25752879:P69:Q2154182",
        "wd:Q25752879:P69:Q81170"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-04T00:00:39Z",
      "text": "He worked for the Columbia University Mailman School of Public Health and the Detroit Health Department, and worked in Detroit.",
      "cites": [
        "wd:Q25752879:P108:Q5149896",
        "wd:Q25752879:P108:Q25000650",
        "wd:Q25752879:P937:Q12439"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-04T00:00:47Z",
      "text": "There is 1 award on record, the Rhodes Scholarship, received in 2009.",
      "cites": [
        "wd:Q25752879:P166:Q1204346"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-04T00:00:57Z",
      "text": "Readers also turned to James Talarico (1,256,040), Democratic Party (United States) (256,501), and United States Senate (255,791).",
      "cites": [
        "views:en:James_Talarico:2026-11-04",
        "views:en:Democratic_Party_(United_States):2026-11-04",
        "views:en:United_States_Senate:2026-11-04"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-04T00:01:06Z",
      "text": "On 4 November 2026, 1,413,749 people read about the article, about 80 times the usual level.",
      "cites": [
        "views:en:Abdul_El-Sayed:2026-11-04",
        "views:en:Abdul_El-Sayed:prior"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-04T00:01:13Z",
      "text": "The article was read in 11 languages, and after English, the most readers were in Arabic (83,284).",
      "cites": [
        "views:en:Abdul_El-Sayed:2026-11-04",
        "views:ar:عبد_الرحمن_السيد:2026-11-04"
      ]
    },
    {
      "t": "2026-11-04T00:01:20Z",
      "text": "On the globe, each language glows where it is mainly spoken, brighter for more readers, and a language is not a country.",
      "cites": [
        "views:ar:عبد_الرحمن_السيد:2026-11-04",
        "views:fr:Abdul_El-Sayed:2026-11-04",
        "views:de:Abdul_El-Sayed:2026-11-04",
